  the reminder was gone (R, P, RC, RF): 1 of 70, a cap under P, and words first 0 of 70. F: 1 of 18. THIS IS NOT A
  READING. It pools arms after seeing them, it was no registered contrast, and at this ceiling the registered one
  could not be run. It is written down because it is the shape the reminder hypothesis predicted, so that the next
  registration can test it: on the failure this world does produce, a second refused stop, not on a gain the ceiling
  leaves no room for.

What the numbers do NOT show. Nothing about any arm: not that R works, not that B fails. Nothing about the served
loop: the unpatched build passed this world's door 22 times of 22 and the served one 4 of 8, so whatever stalls the
served loop at its door is not reproduced by a 55,000-character synthesized skill, a finished plan and a refused
stop alone. Two differences are visible and unmeasured: here the first step's refusal names the next command, and
the segment allows six completions where the served measure allowed one. One world, one model, one effort, and the
